# TARGET ARCHITECTURE: x86_64 | v0.18 | aws/amazon-linux-2023
# Enterprise Linux Audit v0.16 | aws/amazon-linux-2023 | mandatory Tier 2 cloud host controls
# Source context: AWS SSM Agent and EC2 cloud-init; CloudTrail required for API/SG/IAM
# Host auditd cannot observe cloud-native API calls, security-group, IAM or NSG changes initiated remotely.
# Cloud native API logging is a mandatory companion; see Implementation Guide.
# No agent-specific path is assumed installed; missing agent paths MUST be assessed for this image.
# Monitors root daemon automation with unset loginuid (not normal interactive root sessions).
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S execve,execveat -F auid=unset -F euid=0 -k t2_aws_daemon_exec
# Root-owned cloud daemon outbound connections; SOCKADDR does not expose cloud API operation semantics.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S connect -F auid=unset -F euid=0 -k t2_aws_daemon_connect
# Includes cloud-init/guest provisioning edits in /etc; not a substitute for exact agent watches.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc -F perm=wa -F auid=unset -F euid=0 -k t2_aws_root_config
# x86_64 compatibility ABI for daemon execution/connect where 32-bit emulation is enabled.
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S execve,execveat -F auid=unset -F euid=0 -k t2_aws_daemon_exec
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S connect -F auid=unset -F euid=0 -k t2_aws_daemon_connect

# AMI variant matters: AWS publishes amazon-ssm-agent on standard AL2023 AMI,
# not its minimal AMI. awscli-2 appears in standard AND minimal AMIs.
# Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/linux/al2023/ug/image-comparison.html
# AWS path evidence: SSM mutable overrides /etc/amazon/ssm, state /var/lib/amazon/ssm.
# Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 EC2 images may deliver SSM via Snap; package content is
# /snap/amazon-ssm-agent/current (read-only, revisioned). Watch writable
# overrides and agent state instead; /etc/systemd/system covers unit overrides.
# The AWS Snap page currently does NOT establish Ubuntu 26.04 image defaults.
# Sources: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/ssm-agent-technical-details.html
# https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/agent-install-ubuntu-64-snap.html
# CONDITIONAL mandatory coverage: resolve installed paths on the target cloud image.
# The following watches are NOT automatically activated because a missing path may reject the rule.
# If component installed and relevant, activate its exact file/dir watch or document an approved N/A.
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/amazon/ssm -F perm=wa -k t2_aws_agent_conf
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/cloud -F perm=wa -k t2_aws_agent_conf
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/var/lib/amazon/ssm -F perm=wa -k t2_aws_agent_conf
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F path=/root/.aws/credentials -F perm=wa -k t2_aws_agent_conf
# -a always,exit -F path=/usr/bin/aws -F perm=x -k t2_aws_cli
